      "story_intro": "织机巷的冬夜，两道梭光沿斜角对穿，在庭心打了个解不开的光结——夜巡把考点就定在结上：蛋在交叉处，两条径同时把寒意送进庭心。塔要学的不是堵，而是同时照住两个方向。",
      "story_intro_en": "On a winter night in Weft Lane two shuttle-lights crossed the alleys diagonally and tied an untying knot at the court's heart — the watch set the exam right on that knot: the egg at the crossing, both lanes pushing cold into the court at once. What the towers must learn here is not to wall, but to cover two directions in the same breath.",
      "story_outro": "光结在寅时自己解开，分成两股温顺的灯河退回巷口。夜巡使记下：十字可守，去葫芦腰——那里光要收进一线。",
      "story_outro_en": "At the third watch the light-knot untied itself and flowed back down the alleys as two docile rivers of lamp. The marshal noted: the cross can be held — now to the Gourd Waist, where light must be drawn into a single thread."
    },
